{"name":"Healthy Wealthy and Wise","hex":"#d2dcce","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"healthy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Enjoying good health; free from disease or disorder.","Conducive to health."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/healthy"},{"term":"wealthy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Possessing financial wealth; rich.","Abundant in quality or quantity; profuse. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of rich: the wealthy people of a society or of the world collectively.","A rich person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wealthy"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\nUsed simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nSimply connecting two clauses or sentences. \n\nIntroducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first.","Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"}],"entries":[{"title":"Healthy, Wealthy and Wise","blocks":[{"text":"Healthy, Wealthy and Wise is an Australian lifestyle television program. It was originally broadcast on Network Ten from 1992 until 1998. The show was created and produced by Michael Dickinson. Gavan Disney, once the producer of the Nine Network's long-running variety show Hey Hey it's Saturday, served as executive producer and the show was packaged by Disney Entertainment P/L for the Ten Network and its affiliates throughout the world."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Healthy%2C_Wealthy_and_Wise","wikidata":"Q17006337"},{"title":"Health","blocks":[{"text":"Health has a variety of definitions which have been used for different purposes over time and is a multidimensional concept. It commonly refers to physical and emotional well-being. Good health is associated with normal functioning of the human body in day to day life, absent of disease, pain, or injury."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Health","wikidata":"Q12147"},{"title":"Wealth","blocks":[{"text":"Wealth is the abundance of valuable financial assets or physical possessions which can be converted into a form that can be used for transactions. This includes the core meaning as held in the originating Old English word weal, which is from the Indo-European word stem, wel-, meaning \"to wish\" or \"good\". The modern concept of wealth is of significance in all areas of economics, and clearly so for growth economics and development economics, yet the meaning of wealth is context-dependent. A person possessing a substantial net worth is known as wealthy. Net worth is defined as the current value of one's assets less liabilities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/World_map_of_median_wealth_per_adult_by_country._Credit_Suisse._2021_publication.png/330px-World_map_of_median_wealth_per_adult_by_country._Credit_Suisse._2021_publication.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wealth","wikidata":"Q200535"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Smallpox_eradication_team.jpg/500px-Smallpox_eradication_team.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Smallpox_eradication_team.jpg/500px-Smallpox_eradication_team.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Donald Henderson (left) was part of the CDC's smallpox eradication team in 1966","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmallpox_eradication_team.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Overweight_or_obese_population_OECD_2010.png/500px-Overweight_or_obese_population_OECD_2010.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Overweight_or_obese_population_OECD_2010.png/500px-Overweight_or_obese_population_OECD_2010.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Percentage of overweight or obese population in 2010. Data source: OECD's iLibrary.[39][40]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOverweight_or_obese_population_OECD_2010.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Obese_population_OECD_2010.png/500px-Obese_population_OECD_2010.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Obese_population_OECD_2010.png/500px-Obese_population_OECD_2010.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Percentage of obese population in 2010. Data source: OECD's iLibrary.[39][41]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AObese_population_OECD_2010.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Drug_ampoule_JPN.jpg/500px-Drug_ampoule_JPN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Drug_ampoule_JPN.jpg/1280px-Drug_ampoule_JPN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Drug_ampoule_JPN.jpg/500px-Drug_ampoule_JPN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern drug ampoules","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADrug_ampoule_JPN.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Nurses_at_Butawin_Urban_Clinic%2C_PNG_%2